  "id": "COMPOUND:29364 - PROTEIN:3049",
  "verbalization": "Oxindole is shown to interact with Sodium/Potassium Transporting ATPase subunits, which are targets of multiple oxindole derivatives, including (4aS,6aR,6aS,6bR,8aR,10S,12aS,14bS)-2,2,6a,6b,9,9,12a-heptamethyl-10-octanoyloxy-13-oxo-3,4,5,6,6a,7,8,8a,10,11,12,14b-dodecahydro-1H-picene-4a-carboxylic acid, (2E,6E)-3,7,11-Trimethyl-9-(phenylsulfonyl)-2,6,10-dodecatrien-1-ol, and 6-O-Acetyldihydrohelenalin. All these compounds share a common target of Cytochrome c4, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Oxindole may influence cellular processes through this pathway. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Oxindole and Cytochrome c4 via the Sodium/Potassium Transporting ATPase subunits, implying a possible role in modulating mitochondrial function or energy homeostasis. The consistent targeting of Cytochrome c4 across different oxindole derivatives strengthens the hypothesis, though further validation is needed to confirm the specific mechanism and biological relevance.",
